  (text "FRONT PANEL: lights, knobs, buttons, screen, card slot\nLEDs: one data line from the Pico runs through the 32x8 grid panel first, then on through the 22 indicator LEDs\n(11 bus lights, 7 key-on lights, 4 Assign lights). Use 5mm through-hole WS2812 LEDs (e.g. WS2812D-F5) for these;\ntheir pin order differs from the WS2812B drawn here, so check the LED's datasheet when wiring.\nFeed the grid's power with thick wires straight from the USB-C connector, not through the protoboard." (at 25.4 22.86 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid fc2d1b80-e135-546e-835f-193534993415)
  )
  (text "KNOBS: 4 potentiometers read by an MCP3204. BUTTONS and the ENCODER: two MCP23017 I2C expanders\nwith their built-in pull-ups turned on in firmware; every button just shorts its pin to ground.\nExpander 0x21 also drives the screen backlight and reset, and the volume chip's select line." (at 25.4 200.66 0)
    (effects (font (size 1.5 1.5)) (justify left top))
    (uuid 7ea7144b-925c-5bc9-8d7e-8e2a0e3ed715)
  )
)
